# zram's backing file. fs_mgr makes /data/per_boot/zram_swap when swapon_all turns the swap
# on (fstab.dsa's zram_backingdev_size, dsa-memory.rc), but only in a folder that exists.
# Android's own init.rc makes /data/per_boot only once the boot has completed, after zram is
# on, so the folder is made here first, in exactly the way init.rc makes it: the last boot's
# folder goes, then a new one with the key that lasts for this boot alone (per_boot_ref), so
# nothing zram wrote outlives the boot it was swapped out in. init.rc repeats both steps when
# the boot completes; the backing file it then removes stays open, and in use, until Android
# stops. The same owner and key matter: init asks for a wipe of the user's data when a folder it
# makes at the top of /data already has another key.
#
# The folder has a type of its own (memory.cil), which init may write, the kernel's loop driver
# may read and write, toolbox's rm (the step above and init.rc's) may empty and remove, and
# nothing else may open.
#
# A system script, because only init itself may make a folder at the top of /data; init's
# vendor scripts run as vendor_init, which may not. It runs after init.rc's own post-fs-data
# steps, which install the keys.
on post-fs-data
    exec - system system -- /bin/rm -rf /data/per_boot
    mkdir /data/per_boot 0700 system system encryption=Require key=per_boot_ref
    restorecon_recursive /data/per_boot
